{"availability":"available","full":"heychristoph/soc2-auditor","name":"soc2-auditor","description":"A skill to perform a SOC 2 audit on a given org","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-29T12:08:23Z","updated":"2026-10-02T13:47:09Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":null,"color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Example AI Audit report: DoneThat SOC 2 Type 1.","An agent skill that runs an AI Audit modeled on a SOC 2 Type 1 or Type 2 examination: it pulls evidence from the client's compliance platform, tests every control against the Trust Services Criteria, and produces a PDF signed by the model that ran it. The report says it is an AI Audit, not an official SOC 2 audit.","It follows the open Agent Skills format, so the same soc2-audit/ folder works with Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, Cursor, GitHub Copilot and other agents that read SKILL.md. All deterministic work runs in plain Python scripts, so nothing depends on one vendor's agent features."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/heychristoph/soc2-auditor/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"dfd0ba93348bd3519361fdb17eed64edc5b1c0926a28514f15d82ac659f2076e","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Example AI Audit report: DoneThat SOC 2 Type 1.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/heychristoph/soc2-auditor/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"dfd0ba93348bd3519361fdb17eed64edc5b1c0926a28514f15d82ac659f2076e","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/heychristoph/soc2-auditor/blob/main/R